{"code_citation":"Fla. Stat. § 720.303","title":"Association powers and duties; meetings of board; official records","category":"records","body":"The board of directors shall maintain official records, including all written records of the association, financial reports, and minutes of all meetings, for at least 7 years. The records shall be available for inspection by any member or member's authorized agent within 10 business days after receipt of written request. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text from leg.state.fl.us before production use.","source_url":"http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0700-0799/0720/Sections/0720.303.html","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Fla. Stat. § 720.305","title":"Obligations of members; remedies at law or in equity; levy of fines and suspension of use rights","category":"fines","body":"The association may levy reasonable fines of up to $100 per violation against any member or any tenant, guest, or invitee. No fine may exceed $1,000 in the aggregate unless otherwise provided in the governing documents. A fine of $1,000 or more may become a lien against the parcel. A fine or suspension may not be imposed without at least 14 days' written notice and an opportunity for a hearing before a committee of at least 3 members appointed by the board who are not officers, directors, or employees of the association, or the spouse, parent, child, brother, or sister of such persons. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0700-0799/0720/Sections/0720.305.html","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Fla. Stat. § 720.3085","title":"Payment for assessments; lien claims","category":"foreclosure","body":"When authorized by the governing documents, the association has a lien on each parcel to secure the payment of assessments and other amounts provided for in this section. The lien is effective from the date of recording in the public records. The association may bring an action in its name to foreclose a lien for unpaid assessments in the manner a mortgage of real property is foreclosed. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0700-0799/0720/Sections/0720.3085.html","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Fla. Stat. § 720.306","title":"Meetings of members; voting and election procedures; amendments","category":"meetings","body":"The members of the association shall hold an annual meeting. Notice of the annual meeting must be mailed, delivered, or electronically transmitted to the members not less than 14 days before the date of the meeting. Special meetings of the members may be called by the president, by a majority of the board, or upon written request of 10 percent of the total voting interests. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0700-0799/0720/Sections/0720.306.html","effective_date":null}
